1
00:00:06,093 --> 00:00:10,216
Every act of knowing seems to come
with a small distance built in.

2
00:00:11,044 --> 00:00:13,573
Here is a subject. There is an object.

3
00:00:13,653 --> 00:00:17,336
And behind the appearing, a
ground that it all rests on.

4
00:00:17,416 --> 00:00:20,393
If knowing always carries this structure,

5
00:00:20,473 --> 00:00:24,755
then every taste of presence is
already filtered through a gap.

6
00:00:24,835 --> 00:00:27,893
Adding one more act of
knowing will not close it.

7
00:00:27,973 --> 00:00:29,963
That act would carry the gap with it.

8
00:00:30,786 --> 00:00:34,511
The tradition's answer is not to
build a bridge across the gap.

9
00:00:34,591 --> 00:00:37,473
It is that the gap was
never holding anything up.

10
00:00:37,553 --> 00:00:39,918
When the standing behind is seen through,

11
00:00:39,998 --> 00:00:43,030
no witness is placed
apart from what appears.

12
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:46,712
No ground remains that appearances
must be checked against.

13
00:00:46,792 --> 00:00:50,453
What remains is the immediacy
of appearing itself.

14
00:00:51,286 --> 00:00:54,236
This is why experience
can be vivid and direct.

15
00:00:54,316 --> 00:00:58,666
Vividness here is not intensity
added to ordinary perception.

16
00:00:58,746 --> 00:01:03,733
It is the absence of the mediation that
usually makes perception feel distant.

17
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:08,244
And the emptiness that applies to the
dull applies equally to the vivid.

18
00:01:08,324 --> 00:01:11,356
Immediacy does not make
appearances more real.

19
00:01:11,436 --> 00:01:14,580
It describes how they are no
longer held at a distance.

20
00:01:15,397 --> 00:01:18,931
Longchenpa speaks of the
self-liberation of thought.

21
00:01:19,011 --> 00:01:21,879
It describes the same thing
from the side of thinking.

22
00:01:21,959 --> 00:01:24,406
Thoughts arise, and are not followed.

23
00:01:24,486 --> 00:01:28,093
And because they are not followed,
they do not become a wall.

24
00:01:28,926 --> 00:01:32,750
Then comes a question. Is this
an achievement, or a stopping?

25
00:01:33,573 --> 00:01:37,718
If the gap is a construction,
its absence is a stopping.

26
00:01:37,798 --> 00:01:41,346
The taste is there wherever the
construction is not running.

27
00:01:41,426 --> 00:01:45,449
If the gap were built into things,
the taste would be impossible.

28
00:01:45,529 --> 00:01:47,936
Practice would only show the gap again.

29
00:01:48,016 --> 00:01:51,917
Madhyamaka and Dzogchen
both take the first view.

30
00:01:51,997 --> 00:01:54,213
That leaves two things to understand.

31
00:01:54,293 --> 00:01:57,012
Why does the construction
return so readily?

32
00:01:57,092 --> 00:01:59,883
And what, in practice, loosens it?

33
00:02:00,697 --> 00:02:02,550
One caution belongs here.

34
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:07,111
"No gap, no ground" can
quietly become a new ground.

35
00:02:07,191 --> 00:02:10,617
It can turn into a confident
picture of non-duality,

36
00:02:10,697 --> 00:02:12,646
something to possess.

37
00:02:13,458 --> 00:02:16,449
So the immediacy is best described simply.

38
00:02:16,529 --> 00:02:20,145
It appears when the standing
behind is not being kept up.

39
00:02:20,225 --> 00:02:22,975
It is not a state anyone
can now be sure of.

